  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Tie Xue Leng recalls a younger ambition to capture criminals and fill the Demon Suppression Tower.",
      "chapters": [
        176
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_tie_xue_leng"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Standing tall in the Tie Clan mountain fort, the tower imprisons countless demonic Gu Masters and is named the symbol of the righteous faction.",
      "chapters": [
        182
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_tie_clan",
        "sys_demonic_path"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "On Wan Cheng Mountain’s peak area it is a majestic steel tower whose aura is framed as holding up the heavens and stepping on the mountains, with white clouds around it like mist so the tower is seen in a foggy image. The tower is over three hundred metres tall with almost a hundred floors, rustic and ancient in design, and overflowing with righteousness. It is famous not only in the southern borders but all over the world, and even in middle continent many people know of it. Since it was built, hundreds, thousands, and even ten thousand demonic Gu Masters have been imprisoned by Tie clan. Tie Ruo Nan places that tower on Wan Cheng mountain peak when she vows to walk her father’s path.",
      "chapters": [
        211
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_wan_cheng_mountain",
        "char_tie_ruo_nan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In Shang Clan City, crowds call Tie clan’s famous demon suppression tower the nemesis of the demonic path and say Tie clan has captured demonic Gu Masters from everywhere.",
      "chapters": [
        294
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "consequences-for-the-demonic-path",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_shang_clan_city"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A market story names a demonic Gu Master captured by Tie clan and thrown into the demon suppression tower after Gui Ku cave was destroyed.",
      "chapters": [
        328
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "consequences-for-the-demonic-path",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_gui_ku_cave"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After the bronze hall clash, Tie Ruo Nan tells Fang Yuan that if he surrenders she will send him into the Tie clan Demon Suppression Tower to undergo reform, leave later, work for Tie clan, and repay his sins on the righteous path.",
      "chapters": [
        397
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "consequences-for-the-demonic-path",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "She later repeats surrender terms that include entering the Demon Suppression Tower for reform as the only way he can keep his life.",
      "chapters": [
        403
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "consequences-for-the-demonic-path",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan tells Tie Ruo Nan that Lu Zuan Feng has been causing havoc at Tie clan and even infiltrating Demon Suppression Tower. Tie clan higher-ups treat that infiltration as a disturbance: narration calls the tower a renowned prison for the demonic path, yet Lu Zuan Feng entered and left as he pleased, and Tie clan kept the humiliation secret from top clans such as Wu clan and Shang clan.",
      "chapters": [
        359
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "lu-zuan-fengs-infiltrations",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_lu_zuan_feng",
        "fac_wu_clan",
        "fac_shang_clan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan later judges that Lu Zuan Feng should already have repeatedly infiltrated the tower and caused great havoc, leaving Tie clan under huge pressure.",
      "chapters": [
        365
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "lu-zuan-fengs-infiltrations",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "A later Southern Border account again says Lu Zuan Feng had once sneaked into Tie clan’s Demon Suppression Tower.",
      "chapters": [
        965
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "lu-zuan-fengs-infiltrations",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_southern_border"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Tie Mian Shen says the clan’s Demon Suppression Tower once contained a Seven Illusions Demon Immortal, and that Tie clan learned many secrets of that true inheritance without obtaining its contents.",
      "chapters": [
        1340
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "seven-illusions-imprisonment",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_tie_mian_shen"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Among Southern Border super forces, Tie clan is named the force that targeted the demonic path most fiercely, especially after building the Demon Suppression Tower, as a pillar of the righteous path in pursuing demonic path Gu Immortals.",
      "chapters": [
        1341
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "seven-illusions-imprisonment",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fairy Miao Yin contrasts Southern Border’s Tie clan Demon Suppression Tower as excelling at imprisonment with Heavenly Court’s Demon Judgment Board methods.",
      "chapters": [
        2062
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "seven-illusions-imprisonment",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fairy_miao_yin",
        "fac_heavenly_court",
        "house_demon_judgment_board"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Tie Ruo Nan says she was in closed cultivation inside Demon Suppression Tower and consulted clan seniors there about immortal ascension.",
      "chapters": [
        2263
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "closed-cultivation",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
